window.docContents[222].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___33-Maclaurin-Series-and-Laurent-Series/#chapter-4-section-33":{"contents":"Source: NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, §4.33.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions","header":"4.33. §4.33 Maclaurin Series and Laurent Series","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___33-Maclaurin-Series-and-Laurent-Series/#chapter-4-section-33"},"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___16-Mathematical-Applications/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications--Number-theoretic-significance-of-li_LPAR_x_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\n\n\nThe source note records that Figure 6.16.2 was produced at NIST.\n\nAssuming the named Mathlib proposition RiemannHypothesis for the nonreal\nzeros of ζ, the canonical map realLogarithmicIntegral supplies the\nprincipal-value logarithmic integral through its §6.2 characterization.  Mathlib's\nprimeCountingReal x = Nat.primeCounting ⌊x⌋₊ counts primes not exceeding x;\nthis is the real-variable specialization appropriate to the source's\nx → ∞ statement.  The source points to\n§25.10(i), §27.12,\nFigure 6.16.2, and Bays–Hudson (2000).\n\n\\operatorname{li}(x)-\\pi(x)=O(\\sqrt{x}\\ln x),\\quad x\\to\\infty$$\n\nFigure 6.16.2 compares li(x) with the step values of π(x) for\nx=10,20,…,1000; it is an NIST-produced graph, as noted by the source.\n\nFigure 6.16.2: logarithmic integral with vertical bars marking prime counts.\n\nend LMLFManual.Chapter6\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.16 Mathematical Applications\u0009§6.16 Mathematical Applications","header":"Number-theoretic significance of li(x)","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___16-Mathematical-Applications/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications--___6___16-Mathematical-Applications--Number-theoretic-significance-of-li_LPAR_x_RPAR_"}});